  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final text sets a 6.5% permanent S2 failure ceiling with no sales stop, which lets Hearth 10 (6.2%) remain on sale and is the main concession to Northwind. S3 gives a 6-year retrofit for installed units, which benefits Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage, while S5 makes an 8-per-100k recall mandatory, counting unreported incidents, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) though corrective action can replace permanent withdrawal. S1 sets a 24-hour reporting deadline that is strict for both companies given their unreported incidents."
